The adaptor is an original work of nodemode-ai: one family spec built from
formcompiler's registry, each repository's visibility and each public app's
released tag, and pull requests that keep every target repository's generated
files in step with it.

The scripts use the Python standard library only. The workflows call
third-party GitHub Actions under their own licences, run on CI runners only and
never distributed: actions/checkout and actions/create-github-app-token (MIT),
and rhysd/actionlint in the self-check (MIT).
